{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me try one more approach. Maybe I should try to create a more sophisticated sampling strategy to give the model better context, or maybe try to use a different transformation approach:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_03dad10005ba4a5a8295d300","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"pipeline.py","content":"\"\"\"Candidate data pipeline around a FROZEN tabular foundation model.\n\nThe harness calls, in order:\n  1. preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test)        -> X_train, y_train, X_test   (cleaning, target transform)\n  2. engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test)          -> X_train, X_test            (feature engineering, <= 500 cols)\n  3. sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows)  -> list of index arrays       (context views; each view is fit separately\n                                                                                 and predictions are averaged)\n  4. frozen model fit/predict per view (never edit this part; MODEL_KWARGS tunes the constructor)\n  5. postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test)     -> pred                       (invert target transforms, calibrate)\n\n`pred` is a pandas DataFrame of class probabilities (columns = class labels) for classification, or a\npandas Series for regression. `y_train_orig` is the untransformed training target. All inputs are pandas\nobjects; X_train / X_test share columns. Do not read any file other than the ones in this directory.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nMODEL_KWARGS = {}  # constructor settings for the frozen model; {} keeps the defaults\n\n\ndef preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Apply log transformation to skewed features\n    X_train = X_train.copy()\n    X_test = X_test.copy()\n    \n    # Log transform skewed features (Insulin has high skewness)\n    if 'Insulin' in X_train.columns:\n        X_train['Insulin'] = np.log1p(X_train['Insulin'])\n        X_test['Insulin'] = np.log1p(X_test['Insulin'])\n    \n    return X_train, y_train, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Create domain-specific features\n    X_train = X_train.copy()\n    X_test = X_test.copy()\n    \n    # Add ratio features that are medically relevant\n    X_train['glucose_bmi_ratio'] = X_train['Glucose'] / (X_train['BMI'] + 1e-8)\n    X_test['glucose_bmi_ratio'] = X_test['Glucose'] / (X_test['BMI'] + 1e-8)\n    \n    return X_train, X_test\n\n\ndef sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows):\n    # Create multiple context views for better generalization\n    n_views = 3\n    indices = np.arange(len(X_train))\n    np.random.shuffle(indices)\n    \n    # Split data into multiple views\n    view_size = len(X_train) // n_views\n    views = []\n    for i in range(n_views):\n        start_idx = i * view_size\n        end_idx = len(X_train) if i == n_views - 1 else (i + 1) * view_size\n        views.append(indices[start_idx:end_idx])\n    \n    return views\n\n\ndef postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test):\n    return pred"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":10080,"output":716,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10796,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791011325816,"responseId":"chatcmpl-9ce3fe37c954b85b","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","thinkingLevel":"off"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_03dad10005ba4a5a8295d300","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote to pipeline.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791011329352}]}
